# 11. Complete workflow testing plan

After the fixes, the application should pass the following end-to-end tests.

| Workflow            | Test                                      | Required outcome                                                  |
| ------------------- | ----------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------- |
| Employee login      | Login and navigate between screens        | Session remains valid and screens use current permissions         |
| Employee management | Create employee and log in                | Profile and login both exist and are consistent                   |
| Product management  | Add or update product                     | Saved product appears immediately                                 |
| Stock management    | Receive stock and issue stock to salesman | Both balances and ledger update correctly                         |
| Production          | Create and approve a batch                | Raw materials are deducted exactly once                           |
| Packaging           | Package bulk production                   | Bulk stock decreases and the correct packet SKUs increase         |
| Dispatch            | Dispatch packets to a salesman            | Factory stock decreases and salesman stock increases exactly once |
| Sales               | Create a bill                             | Sale, payment, stock, and invoice remain consistent               |
| Sale retry          | Retry a timed-out request                 | Existing transaction is recovered without duplication             |
| Expenses            | Submit and approve expense                | Status and cash reconciliation update                             |
| Daily closing       | Submit and review closing                 | Figures match the underlying financial records                    |
| Salary              | Calculate incentive                       | Amount matches authoritative eligible sales and configured policy |
| Salary payment      | Approve and pay salary                    | Status changes only after backend confirmation                    |
| Dashboard           | Complete sales and stock operations       | Relevant metrics update without a hard refresh                    |
| Reports             | Change a business record                  | Relevant reports display current saved data                       |
| Recovery            | Simulate a failed secondary write         | Incomplete transaction is identified and safely recoverable       |

### Test the failure cases, not just the successful cases

For production and financial workflows, the critical test is often what happens when the network fails between two writes.

For every multi-step transaction, simulate failure after each individual write.

Then verify that the application can recover without duplicate stock movements, duplicate payments, or incorrect salary records.

